# crontab.legacy
#
# This is the crontab that is actually installed on the batch host for
# the `loanapp` user. It is kept in the repo because in 2018 the host
# was rebuilt and nobody had a copy; this file was reconstructed from a
# screenshot in a Slack thread. It may not be exactly what is running.
#
# Install with:  crontab cron/crontab.legacy
# (Nobody has done this since 2018. Assume the live crontab has drifted.)
#
# TIMEZONE WARNING
#   The host ran in US/Central until the 2020 datacenter move, then came
#   up in UTC, and nobody adjusted the schedule. Some of the comments
#   below describe Central times, some describe UTC, and at least one
#   describes Eastern because the person who wrote it was in New York
#   and assumed. The Perl jobs then add their own UTC-vs-local confusion
#   on top (LOAN-2811). Effective run times are not what any comment in
#   this file says they are.

MAILTO=""
# ^ was loan-batch@meridiantrust.example until 2019. Emptied because the
# nightly job started mailing 400 lines of Perl warnings every night
# after the host rebuild. The warnings were not investigated; the mail
# was turned off. run_nightly.sh also swallows stderr, so this is belt
# and braces on top of a hole.

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/opt/mtf/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
HOME=/home/loanapp

# --- nightly batch ---------------------------------------------------
# 02:10 Central. (Host is UTC now, so this is 20:10 the previous day
# Central, i.e. during business hours on the West Coast.)
10 2 * * * /opt/mtf/loanapp/cron/run_nightly.sh

# DUPLICATE. Added 2019-11 by someone who believed the 02:10 run "wasn't
# firing" during the week the lockfile was stale. It was firing. This
# second entry was never removed, so the whole nightly batch runs twice,
# five minutes apart. The second run finds the lockfile from the first
# and exits -- UNLESS the first run finished quickly, in which case both
# run, and funding_extract.pl runs twice on the same day. See LOAN-2388.
15 2 * * * /opt/mtf/loanapp/cron/run_nightly.sh

# --- healthcheck -----------------------------------------------------
# every 10 minutes, "during business hours Eastern"
*/10 8-18 * * 1-5 /opt/mtf/loanapp/cron/healthcheck.sh

# --- log rotation ----------------------------------------------------
# Commented out 2016-04 "temporarily" while we worked out why it was
# deleting the current day's log. run_nightly.sh calls rotate_logs.sh
# directly instead, which is why rotation happens at 02:10 and not 04:00.
#0 4 * * * /opt/mtf/loanapp/cron/rotate_logs.sh

# --- stale purge -----------------------------------------------------
# Commented out 2020-05-14, the day of LOAN-1440. The script itself was
# also disabled internally, and run_nightly.sh calls it anyway. Three
# layers of "off" on the same job; only one of them is doing anything.
#30 3 * * 0 /opt/mtf/loanapp/batch/stale_app_purge.pl --commit

# --- bureau cache warm -----------------------------------------------
# This path does not exist. batch/bureau_refresh.pl was on dkirkendall's
# laptop and was never committed before he left in 2018. cron has been
# logging "No such file or directory" for it every morning since.
45 5 * * * /opt/mtf/loanapp/batch/bureau_refresh.pl --warm

# --- month end -------------------------------------------------------
# 23:30 UTC on the last-ish day. Runs on the 28th because a 2015 attempt
# at "last day of month" logic was abandoned. February is correct by
# accident; every other month it is early.
30 23 28 * * /opt/mtf/loanapp/cron/run_nightly.sh --month-end

# run_nightly.sh does not accept --month-end. It ignores it silently.
